00:17:02.000 --> 00:17:06.000
The reason for prompt management was

00:17:06.000 --> 00:17:10.000
If you hard code your prompt

00:17:10.000 --> 00:17:14.000
Then you have to change the system prompt

00:17:14.000 --> 00:17:18.000
When your application is in production

00:17:18.000 --> 00:17:22.000
Then you have to redeploy the whole application

00:17:22.000 --> 00:17:26.000
You have to trigger the deployment pipeline again

00:17:26.000 --> 00:17:30.000
What is the way to avoid that

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:34.000
You should not hard code your system prompt

00:17:34.000 --> 00:17:38.000
What piece of information you are attaching to your code

00:17:38.000 --> 00:17:42.000
Which prompt you have to load

00:17:42.000 --> 00:17:46.000
And what should be its respective label

00:17:46.000 --> 00:17:50.000
And your lang fuse will automatically go to your server

00:17:50.000 --> 00:17:54.000
Where you have a prompt in a database

00:17:54.000 --> 00:17:58.000
It will bring your prompt through an API call

00:17:58.000 --> 00:18:02.000
And this prompt will be dynamically injected into your code

00:18:02.000 --> 00:18:06.000
The simple thing of prompt management is

00:18:06.000 --> 00:18:10.000
You can make your code flexible

00:18:10.000 --> 00:18:14.000
So that you don't have to redeploy with every prompt change

00:18:14.000 --> 00:18:18.000
