So there are 2 key technical terms

00:28:34.000 --> 00:28:38.000
First is your promotion

00:28:38.000 --> 00:28:42.000
You can call it version promotion or prompt promotion

00:28:42.000 --> 00:28:46.000
What happens in version promotion is that you shift your label

00:28:46.000 --> 00:28:50.000
On the next version

00:28:50.000 --> 00:28:54.000
A good example of this is your latest label

00:28:54.000 --> 00:28:58.000
Latest label is a default label

00:28:58.000 --> 00:29:02.000
This is a default label and Langfuse uses it internally

00:29:02.000 --> 00:29:06.000
I have shown you in the last class as well, we didn't use latest

00:29:06.000 --> 00:29:10.000
We didn't attach it with our prompt but with our latest prompt

00:29:10.000 --> 00:29:14.000
So this label was attached

00:29:14.000 --> 00:29:18.000
Latest is attached with the newest version of the prompt

00:29:18.000 --> 00:29:22.000
So if I have V1, V2, V3, then with V3, the latest will be attached

00:29:22.000 --> 00:29:26.000
Tomorrow I will make some changes in my prompt, it will be V4

00:29:26.000 --> 00:29:30.000
So with this V4, the latest will be attached automatically

00:29:30.000 --> 00:29:34.000
I don't need to shift it, so this is called promotion

00:29:34.000 --> 00:29:38.000
What happens in promotion is that you shift the labels in the next version

00:29:38.000 --> 00:29:42.000
Automatically, you are promoting the versions

00:29:42.000 --> 00:29:46.000
And one is your rollback

00:29:46.000 --> 00:29:50.000
Rollback means that you are going back one or two steps

00:29:50.000 --> 00:29:54.000
You are using an old version again

00:29:54.000 --> 00:29:58.000
Like sometimes we update an app or OS

00:29:58.000 --> 00:30:02.000
So there are some glitches or errors

00:30:02.000 --> 00:30:06.000
Or we update drivers, drivers have a lot of them

00:30:06.000 --> 00:30:10.000
So we go back to the previous version

00:30:10.000 --> 00:30:14.000
So if you have tested your application in V3 or V4

00:30:14.000 --> 00:30:18.000
